# pvpgn/conf/address_translation.conf.example
#
# Reference only. You do NOT edit this file by hand for the container build:
# entrypoint.sh GENERATES /usr/local/pvpgn/etc/pvpgn/address_translation.conf
# at startup from PVPGN_PUBLIC_IP and PVPGN_LOCAL_CIDR. This example just
# documents the format bnetd expects, so you can reason about split-horizon
# behaviour or hand-write it for a native (non-container) install.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS (split-horizon NAT for the w3route port):
#   Warcraft III matchmaking hands each client a host address for the w3route
#   relay. Clients on your LAN must be told the server's INTERNAL address;
#   clients coming in over the internet must be told your PUBLIC (WAN) address.
#   bnetd picks per client based on which network the client's source IP falls
#   in, using the rules below.
#
# Reference: github.com/pvpgn/pvpgn-server, conf/address_translation.conf.in.
#
# FORMAT (whitespace-separated columns):
#   input(ip:port)   output(ip:port)   exclude(net)   include(net)
#
#   input    the local listen address:port bnetd matches on (w3route port).
#            0.0.0.0 means "any local interface on this port".
#   output   the address:port to advertise to a client that this rule applies
#            to. Set this to YOUR public/WAN IP.
#   exclude  a client network that this rule does NOT apply to. Clients whose
#            source IP is inside this network are NOT given the output address
#            (they keep the server's internal address). Put your LAN/RFC1918
#            ranges here so local clients stay on the internal path.
#   include  a client network the rule DOES apply to. ANY = everyone not
#            excluded (i.e. the public internet).
#
# EXAMPLE (public IP shown is the RFC-5737 documentation range; replace with
# your own WAN IP, and replace the exclude nets with your own LAN ranges):
#
# input             output              exclude            include
0.0.0.0:6200        203.0.113.10:6200   192.168.0.0/16     ANY
0.0.0.0:6200        203.0.113.10:6200   10.0.0.0/8         ANY
0.0.0.0:6200        203.0.113.10:6200   172.16.0.0/12     ANY
